{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:10RangeTrees15LazySegmentTreeV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LazySegmentTree","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"LazySegmentTree","remoteSource":{"fileName":"LazySegmentTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree.swift#L31"},"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LazySegmentTree","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"RangeTrees"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"A segment tree with lazy propagation: a sequence of values that combines any range of them","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"under a monoid and applies an update to every value in a range, each in O(log ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Segment-trees","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree"],"generated":true,"title":"Segment trees"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/rangetrees\/lazysegmenttree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text"